<title>CHINA: China's Beijing Jeep '96 profits 260 mln yuan.</title>
<headline>China's Beijing Jeep '96 profits 260 mln yuan.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Beijing Jeep Corp, a joint venture between Beijing Automotive Corp and Chrysler Corp of the United States, made 260 million yuan ($31.3 million) in profits in 1996, the Beijing Economic Daily said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The newspaper did not give comparative figures and did not say whether the figure was pre-tax.</p>
<p>Sales reached 5.5 billion yuan in 1996, it said, but gave no further details.</p>
<p>The joint venture produces Cherokee jeeps and Chinese-designed BJ2020 jeeps.</p>
<p>($1 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
</text>
